# Project
Expo + TypeScript mobile client for the Hunt Rewards NestJS API (location-based rewards for restaurants/bars).
Two roles in one app: OWNER and USER. Role comes from GET /auth/me after login.

# Stack (do not swap)
- Expo Router (file-based), route groups: (auth), (user), (owner)
- TanStack Query for all server state; Zustand only for auth/session
- Axios instance in src/api/client.ts with Bearer token interceptor + 401 → logout
- Typed API generated by Orval into src/api/generated — never hand-write request/response types
- Token stored in expo-secure-store, never AsyncStorage
- NativeWind for styling; react-hook-form + zod for forms
- Base URL from EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL

# API facts
- Swagger JSON: {API_URL}/api-json (source of truth for shapes)
- Media flow: POST /upload (multipart) → Cloudinary URL → send URL to /submissions, /venues, /perks
- Points are per venue (GET /users/me/points)
- Approval awards points; redemption returns a promo code

# Conventions
- Feature folders: src/features/<feature>/{hooks,components,screens}
- One query hook per endpoint, with query keys in src/api/keys.ts
- Every screen handles loading, empty, and error states
- Invalidate related queries after mutations (e.g. review → submissions + points)
- No `any`. Keep components under ~200 lines.